<!-- ===== Home pane (P23-5: gen-time-sanitized content panels folded in from
     docs-site — see docs-site/home-fragments.yaml for the content contract
     and internal/scoreboard/view/home.go / portal.go for the security
     rationale of injecting {{.HomePanelsHTML}} unescaped. This is now the
     ONLY place in this template that intentionally bypasses
     esc()/html/template auto-escaping — every other dynamic value in this
     file keeps going through esc() or template.JS exactly as before P23-5.
     (The Story pane's {{.StoryPanelHTML}} injection, the second such site
     as of P23 portal-redesign, was REMOVED in portal-header-refine item 7
     — see portal.go's StoryPanelHTML field doc for why the field itself is
     still left in place, just unreferenced here.)
     (portal-ui-polish: this pane's outer "chassis" — the bespoke inline
     style="padding:...;max-width:..." wrapper + inline-styled <h1>/<p> —
     is replaced with the SAME .p-shell / .p-h1 / header/.brand primitives
     #pane-story / #pane-scoreboard / #pane-me / #pane-terminal already
     share (see the "Shared pane component classes" block above), so all
     five panes now sit in one visually consistent shell. Content INSIDE
     #pane-home-panels — the {{.HomePanelsHTML}} fragments and the static
     参考サイト links below — is unchanged.) ===== -->
<div class="pane p-shell" id="pane-home">

  <header>
    <div class="brand">
      <h1 class="p-h1"><span class="accent">Home</span></h1>
    </div>
  </header>

  <p class="home-intro">統合ポータルへようこそ。上部のタブから進めてください。</p>
  <ul class="home-intro-list">
    <li><strong>Story</strong> — ミッションの流れを追う</li>
    <li><strong>Scoreboard</strong> — 自分のリアルタイムな進捗を確認する</li>
    <li><strong>Terminal</strong> — 実際に手を動かす</li>
  </ul>
  <div id="pane-home-panels">{{.HomePanelsHTML}}
    <!-- 参考サイト (portal-header-refine, item 6): plain hand-authored static
         links, NOT routed through docs-site/home-fragments.yaml's sanitizer
         allowlist (deliberately: this is the ONE bit of Home content that is
         NOT gen-time fragment content, so it does not need that pipeline,
         and broadening the fragment sanitizer's allowlist just for two
         static links would be a needless scope increase — same rationale
         the falco.org/github links this replaces previously carried).
         Placed as a sibling INSIDE #pane-home-panels (after the
         gen-time-rendered {{.HomePanelsHTML}} fragments above) purely so it
         inherits the SAME #pane-home-panels .home-panel/.home-panel-body
         CSS scoping already defined above — this <details> element itself
         is still hand-authored markup, not fragment content. -->
    <details class="home-panel">
      <summary>参考サイト</summary>
      <div class="home-panel-body rich-content">
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://falco.org/docs/reference/rules/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Falco Docs</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/falcosecurity/rules/blob/72945ab934b4449a2bc4befe9e9fcdfe6e106090/rules/falco_rules.yaml" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Falco Rules</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</div>

